+++ b/docs/python-sdk.md
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# Embedded Python SDK
+
+`python/mamba_sdk` and `src/python.rs` expose the internal Rust market modules
+through PyO3/maturin. The interface builds instructions and reads chain state;
+it never accepts private keys or submits transactions. Dexter owns signing and
+send authorization, so no API server is needed.
+
+Prefer Dexter's `scripts/setup_mamba.ps1` / `scripts/setup_mamba.sh` for setup.
+Run it again after updating Mamba. A manual Windows build is:
+
+```powershell
+python scripts/prepare_python_build.py
+maturin build --profile dev --locked --interpreter ..\Dexter\.venv\Scripts\python.exe --out target\wheels
+..\Dexter\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install --force-reinstall target\wheels\mamba_sdk-0.1.0-cp310-abi3-win_amd64.whl
+```
+
+`prepare_python_build.py` restores only missing compile-time IDLs at commits
+already pinned in `UPSTREAM_SOURCES.lock`; add `--tests` for upstream test fixtures.
+Python 3.10+ uses the stable ABI. Rust and the host C/C++ linker are required to
+build the wheel. A downloaded GitHub archive needs the same pinned IDL inputs.
+
+```python
+from mamba_sdk import Client, markets
+
+sdk = Client("https://your-rpc")
+route = await sdk.request("route", mint=mint, market_priority="pump_fun,pump_swap")
+plan = await sdk.request("build", side="buy", mint=mint, user=public_key,
+                         lamports=100_000, slippage_pct=5,
+                         priority_micro_lamports=0)
+```
+
+Operations: `route`, `build`, `curve`, `pool_state`, `snapshot`, `token_balance`,
+`quote_buy` (Pump.fun), and `create` (Pump.fun). Instruction bytes cross the Python
+boundary as base64 with public account metas; private keys stay in the application.
+`decode_pump_log` and `price_from_logs` use the same Rust event types.
+
+The SDK verifies RPC genesis hashes, rejects mixed clusters and excludes endpoints
+that cannot be verified. It uses exactly that pool, without ambient mainnet
+fallbacks. PumpSwap discovery supports provider index restrictions and pagination.
+Snapshots, prices and buy quotes use signed effective quote reserves, including
+boosts and fees held in the vault. Pump sells accept exact raw amounts and only
+close a token account when its entire balance is sold. Other market sells support
+integer percentages; exact partial requests must be representable by that interface.
+
+Supported markets follow `Swaps::default_market_priority()` dynamically. The
+binding does not contain a second set of market instruction layouts.
